  "ai_guidance": {
    "use_when": "Use sf-slider to project the shared Slider/Swiper behavior. In the default template, root-class, author style and root-style customize the existing root; root-style wins. Cosmetic-only changes preserve the active slide, focus and Swiper instances and emit sf-updated with updateMode=dom, not slide-change. afterRender(callback) uses the base lifecycle API. The shared adapter uses navigation aria-label as default Swiper a11y messages; explicit a11y messages override them, disabled a11y remains disabled and aria-labelledby retains native precedence. Omitted space-between and speed inherit Framework spacing and duration tokens; explicit numeric attributes remain compatibility overrides. Reduced motion disables transitions and autoplay. Explicit autoplay pauses on focus and document visibility, while non-visible slides stay outside the keyboard order.",
    "do_not": [
      "Do not copy generated ui-smart code",
      "A slide is one meaningful slot item. Bare slot-only wrappers expose their children; attributed card roots remain whole. Whitespace-only text and comments do not become slides. Preserve composite cards inside one item; do not infer grouping from sibling headings or links.",
      "Use existing root-class=sf-slider--content for text/card slides with controls in normal flow; default media overlay is preserved. Dot hit areas inherit semantic UI geometry from the shared Slider CSS.",
      "Pagination inherits shared Slider CSS: inactive contour and current fill use semantic foreground roles; preserve focus-visible, forced-colors and the appropriate backdrop for transparent schemes. Do not create a Smart-only dot palette.",
      "Do not move host data or access decisions into the component"
    ],
